So, what is ROI?

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:41.320
ROI is a tool that allows you to compare the efficiency of one investment to another investment,

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:44.000
thus allowing you to compare apples and oranges.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.040
ROI measures the amount of return an investment generates relative to the amount that you

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.040
invested.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.720
So, this is the formula for return on an investment.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:56.080
Current value of an investment minus the cost divided by the cost.

