return.

01:24:35.100 --> 01:24:39.340
The height represents the total risk, and as you can see, as the number of securities

01:24:39.340 --> 01:24:44.940
in your portfolio increases, the amount of unsystematic risk decreases, where a systematic

01:24:44.940 --> 01:24:48.580
risk persists, and we'll get to that in a bit.

01:24:48.580 --> 01:24:54.260
Essentially by purchasing more securities, you're going with the concept of not putting

01:24:54.260 --> 01:24:56.300
all your eggs in one basket.

01:24:56.300 --> 01:24:59.460
And since you're spreading your risk over the portfolio by choosing companies in different

01:24:59.460 --> 01:25:05.540
sectors and industries, you're able to avoid your portfolio crashing if one of these things

